Fix PHP 8.2 "Creation of dynamic property" deprecation in tmw/fpdm.

Declares $n explicitly instead of relying on implicit dynamic property
creation, and guards a string-offset read in _bin2hex() with ??''.
Without this, PHP 8.2 raises a deprecation notice for FPDM::$n; on any
TYPO3 instance where SYS.exceptionalErrors includes E_DEPRECATED (the
TYPO3 default), that notice is escalated to a fatal exception and PDF
generation crashes with a 500.

Cherry-picked from the (still open, unmerged as of 2026-07-31) upstream
PR: https://github.com/codeshell/fpdm/pull/69
Drop this patch if that PR is ever merged, or once tmw/fpdm ships a
release that declares $n natively.

--- a/src/fpdm.php	2026-07-31 06:50:15.311331303 +0200
+++ b/src/fpdm.php	2026-07-31 06:50:15.313295484 +0200
@@ -113,6 +113,8 @@
 		var $needAppearancesTrue = false;	//boolean, indicates if /NeedAppearances is already set to true
 		var $isUTF8 = false;				//boolean (true for UTF-8, false for ISO-8859-1)
 		
+		protected int $n = 0;
+
         /**
          * Constructor
          *
@@ -1123,7 +1125,7 @@
 			$hex = "";
 			$i = 0;
 			do {
-				$hex .= sprintf("%02X", ord($str[$i]));
+				$hex .= sprintf("%02X", ord($str[$i]??''));
 				$i++;
 			} while ($i < strlen($str));
 			return $hex;
